---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe31.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope and Cash Equivalents" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Three Activity Classifications" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. THE KEY DIVERGENCE — Direct Method Required, Plus a Mandatory Reconciliation" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Why Both Methods Are Effectively Required in Practice" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Classifying Interest and Dividends" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Non-Cash Transactions" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Worked Example — Direct Method Operating Cash Flows" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — the Supplementary Indirect-Method Reconciliation" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Relationship to IAS 7" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div></div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Presenting cash inflows and outflows by activity</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 31 governs the PREPARATION of the CASH FLOW STATEMENT — CLASSIFYING an ENTERPRISE'S cash INFLOWS and OUTFLOWS into OPERATING, INVESTING, and FINANCING activities. WHILE the OVERALL structure is BROADLY converged with IAS 7, THIS Standard's TREATMENT of the DIRECT/indirect method CHOICE is a GENUINELY notable, PRACTICAL divergence (Section 4).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope and Cash Equivalents</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Short-term, highly liquid investments</div><div class="principle">CASH EQUIVALENTS are SHORT-term, HIGHLY liquid INVESTMENTS readily CONVERTIBLE to KNOWN amounts of CASH, subject to an INSIGNIFICANT risk of CHANGES in value — CONSISTENT with IAS 7'S own definition internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Three Activity Classifications</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Operating, investing, and financing</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Category</span><span>Description</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Operating activities</span><span>PRINCIPAL revenue-PRODUCING activities and OTHER activities that are NOT investing or FINANCING</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Investing activities</span><span>ACQUISITION and DISPOSAL of LONG-term assets and OTHER investments not CONSIDERED cash EQUIVALENTS</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Financing activities</span><span>Activities CHANGING the SIZE and COMPOSITION of the ENTERPRISE'S owners' EQUITY and BORROWINGS</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>THE KEY DIVERGENCE — Direct Method Required, Plus a Mandatory Reconciliation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Unlike IAS 7's free choice</div><div class="text-supporting">UNLIKE IAS 7, WHICH permits a FREE choice BETWEEN the DIRECT method (presenting MAJOR classes of GROSS cash receipts/payments) and the INDIRECT method (STARTING from net PROFIT, adjusting for NON-cash items), ASBE No. 31 REQUIRES the DIRECT method for the PRIMARY Cash Flow STATEMENT presentation — BUT ALSO requires a SUPPLEMENTARY reconciliation from NET profit to NET cash flow FROM operating activities (an INDIRECT-method-STYLE schedule) DISCLOSED separately WITHIN the notes.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Why Both Methods Are Effectively Required in Practice</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Combining the transparency of gross cash flows with a profit reconciliation</div><div class="text-supporting">THIS dual REQUIREMENT reflects a DELIBERATE POLICY choice — the DIRECT method PROVIDES readers with GREATER transparency about the ACTUAL gross CASH movements UNDERLYING operating ACTIVITIES, WHILE the SUPPLEMENTARY indirect-METHOD reconciliation HELPS readers UNDERSTAND the RELATIONSHIP between REPORTED net PROFIT and ACTUAL cash generated — a GENUINELY more COMPREHENSIVE practical REQUIREMENT than IAS 7'S own SINGLE-method choice.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Classifying Interest and Dividends</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A more prescriptive classification than IAS 7's flexible approach</div><div class="text-supporting">FOR most NON-financial enterprises, INTEREST and DIVIDENDS RECEIVED are CLASSIFIED as INVESTING activities, WHILE INTEREST and DIVIDENDS PAID are CLASSIFIED as FINANCING activities — a MORE PRESCRIPTIVE approach than IAS 7, WHICH permits GREATER flexibility (interest/DIVIDENDS received MAY be classified as EITHER operating OR investing; interest/DIVIDENDS paid as EITHER operating OR financing).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Non-Cash Transactions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Excluded from the statement, disclosed separately</div><div class="text-supporting">SIGNIFICANT investing and FINANCING transactions that do NOT involve CASH or cash EQUIVALENTS (e.g. a DEBT-to-equity swap — see the COMPANION ASBE No. 12 poster) are EXCLUDED from the CASH FLOW Statement itself, but DISCLOSED SEPARATELY elsewhere in the FINANCIAL statements.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Direct Method Operating Cash Flows</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Presenting gross cash receipts and payments</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Operating activities under the direct method</div><div class="wk-body">A company receives RMB 500,000,000 cash from customers and pays RMB 320,000,000 cash to suppliers and employees during the year.</div><div class="wk-answer">The PRIMARY Cash Flow Statement presents these as SEPARATE GROSS line ITEMS: "cash RECEIVED from customers RMB 500,000,000" and "cash PAID to suppliers and EMPLOYEES RMB 320,000,000," yielding NET cash from OPERATING activities of <strong>RMB 180,000,000</strong>.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — the Supplementary Indirect-Method Reconciliation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Bridging net profit to operating cash flow</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: The mandatory notes-based reconciliation</div><div class="wk-body">Continuing the prior example, the company's net profit for the year is RMB 150,000,000, with RMB 25,000,000 of depreciation and a RMB 5,000,000 increase in working capital requirements.</div><div class="wk-answer">The SUPPLEMENTARY note RECONCILES: net PROFIT RMB 150,000,000 + depreciation RMB 25,000,000 − working CAPITAL increase RMB 5,000,000 = <strong>RMB 170,000,000</strong> (approximating the SAME net operating CASH flow figure, SUBJECT to rounding and OTHER reconciling items) — REQUIRED IN ADDITION to the DIRECT method statement ITSELF.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 31 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Cash flows classified by operating, investing, and financing activities, using the direct method</span><span>A supplementary reconciliation from net profit to net cash flow from operating activities</span><span>Significant non-cash investing and financing transactions</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Classifying a specific cash flow among operating, investing, or financing activities</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Generally minimal — this is primarily a classification and presentation standard</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 7</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 31 vs IAS 7</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 31</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 7</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Method for primary statement</span><span>Direct method REQUIRED</span><span>Free choice between direct and indirect</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Interest/dividend classification</span><span>Prescriptive (investing/financing)</span><span>Flexible policy choice</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">TWO genuinely NOTABLE practical DIVERGENCES — the MANDATORY direct method (WITH a SUPPLEMENTARY reconciliation) and the MORE prescriptive INTEREST/dividend classification.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every cash flow event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Cash inflows/outflows</span><span><span class="badge bc">CFS</span></span><span>Classified by operating, investing, or financing activity</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 30</span><span>Presentation of Financial Statements — supplies the general presentation framework this Standard's cash flow requirements sit within</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Direct method</div><div class="glossary-def">A Cash Flow Statement presentation showing major classes of gross cash receipts and payments, mandatory for ASBE's primary statement.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Indirect method</div><div class="glossary-def">A reconciliation starting from net profit, adjusting for non-cash items, required as a supplementary note disclosure under ASBE.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe31 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
